{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content project-trajectory/LOG.template.md | Select-Object -First 100; @'\nimport subprocess\nc='c1506fa8017a4578984bf576b070280a5f27fc9b'\ns=subprocess.check_output(['git','show',c+':docs/requirements/interfaces.toml']).decode('utf-8')\nfor key in ['IF-065','IF-245','IF-246','IF-283']:\n a=s.index('[interface.'+key+']'); b=s.find('\\\\n[',a+1); print(s[a:b])\n'@ | python -X utf8 -\"","aggregated_output":"# Project Log — Append-only history\r\n\r\nThe durable record for the gated process (see [process.md](process.md) §5):\r\nsitting sign-offs, review verdicts, approved decisions, and session notes append\r\nhere, **newest last**, and are never rewritten. The working surface — what to\r\ndo *next* — lives in [status.md](status.md), which points here; this file is\r\n**evidence, never normative**: a rule or requirement belongs in the process\r\ndoc or a registry, not in a log entry. Entries here and in status.md cite\r\n**stable ids** (OI-n, stage/bar names, dates), never iteration-branch commit\r\nSHAs — sync scrub/collation may rewrite those (process-options.md \"Agent\r\niteration branch & sync\").\r\n\r\n**Entries already written are never re-worded, including their vocabulary.** A\r\nsign-off that recorded a named human certifying `G1` recorded exactly that; a  <!-- check_vocab: allow -->\r\nlater vocabulary change (the stage ladder retired the `G*` tags) does not reach\r\nbackwards, because rewriting an attestation makes the record claim something was\r\nsigned that was not. Read historical rows through the translation in\r\nprocess.md §4.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Sittings\r\n\r\n**A sitting is an occasion, not a rung.** The stage ladder has eight rungs\r\n(`DevStg-Needs` … `DevStg-Release`, process.md §4) and a project holds far fewer\r\nsittings than that — so sittings stay their **own axis** and each row names the\r\n**rung range it certifies**. Add a row when you actually sit; do not pre-create\r\none per rung. Add columns for any active domain hats, and drop a row your\r\ndeliverable does not need.\r\n\r\nKeep the role columns and the `Human` column distinct: the roles record which\r\nhat signed, `Human` records that a **person** looked. Collapsing them loses the\r\nability to answer \"which sittings did a human actually attend?\".\r\n\r\n| Sitting | Rungs certified | Stakeholder | UX/Docs | System Eng | Test Eng | Human |\r\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\r\n| Requirements/UX/Constraints | `DevStg-Needs` → `DevStg-Reqs` | PENDING | PENDING | PENDING | n/a | PENDING |\r\n| Decomposition & Test Coverage | `DevStg-Arch` → `DevStg-Tests` | n/a | n/a | PENDING | PENDING | PENDING |\r\n| Implementation | `DevStg-Impl` | n/a | n/a | PENDING | PENDING | PENDING |\r\n| Release readiness | `DevStg-Release` | n/a | n/a | n/a | PENDING | PENDING |\r\n| Acceptance | `DevStg-Release` (the owner's final read) | PENDING | n/a | n/a | (evidence) | PENDING |\r\n\r\n## Decisions log\r\n\r\n_Approved or executed decisions only — the call, the alternatives passed over,\r\nwhy (one bullet each; cite ids). A decision still **awaiting** a human is an\r\nOpen item in [status.md](status.md), not a log entry._\r\n\r\n## Audit log\r\n\r\n<!-- Append verdict blocks here per process.md §5. Newest at the bottom. -->\r\n\r\n### DRIVER — DevStg-Reqs — Round 1 — <YYYY-MM-DD>\r\nScaffolding created. Starting DevStg-Reqs.\r\n[interface.IF-065]\r\nowner = \"scripts/agent_common\"\r\nrequestors = [\"scripts/agent_loop\", \"scripts/integrate\", \"scripts/session_service\"]\r\nchannel = \"call\"\r\ndata = \"END_STATES, git, head_sha, acquire_lock, release_lock, preflight, parse_map, process_config, load_wi_registry, substantive_working_tree_dirty, write_session_log, commit_telemetry, loop_claimed\"\r\nversion = \"v1\"\r\nstatus = \"Drafted\"\r\n\r\n[interface.IF-245]\r\nrationale = \"\"\"Each provider runner differs in the flags that make it emit structured output, where its final text is, which events carry its usage and how full its context is. Scattered through the launching roles those differences drift apart, so one module answers them per runner and the session layer imports it.\"\"\"\r\nowner = \"scripts/session_adapters\"\r\nrequestors = [\"scripts/session_service\", \"scripts/agent_route\"]\r\nchannel = \"call\"\r\ndata = \"USAGE_KEYS, OTEL_SEMCONV; adapter_for(argv) -> adapter; adapter methods; HOME_VARIABLES, TOKEN_VARIABLES; cli_named(executable), home_env(cli, home)\"\r\nversion = \"v1\"\r\nstatus = \"Drafted\"\r\ncomponent = \"CMP-008\"\r\nnotes = \"\"\"source - the module imports no kit sibling; the only files it touches are the codex last-message temp file it creates and removes, and a codex rollout file it reads by exact thread id under the launch's CODEX_HOME.\"\"\"\r\n\r\n[interface.IF-246]\r\nrationale = \"\"\"Every role that makes a model call needs the same launch, accounting and record, and a role that keeps its own copy of any of them drifts: a usage fix lands in one path and not the others. One service owns the call and its record, and a role hands it only the data it differs by.\"\"\"\r\nowner = \"scripts/session_service\"\r\nrequestors = [\"scripts/agent_loop\", \"scripts/plan_runner\", \"scripts/dispatch\", \"scripts/coordinator/codex_call\"]\r\nchannel = \"call\"\r\ndata = \"Call (including wi and resume), Outcome; act -> Outcome or BlackoutRefused or HooksOffRefused; call(between, report) -> Outcome; through_blackout(launch) -> Outcome; record(report) -> path; spool_dir(root); lane_branch(root); lane_wis(root); is_call_log(name) -> bool; record writes to the primary spool without a commit outside a claimed lane and reports whether its log was spooled, committed, or refused; call_succeeded(outcome) -> bool; keep plan, version, warmer and route_runner(entry)\"\r\nversion = \"v1\"\r\nstatus = \"Drafted\"\r\ncomponent = \"CMP-008\"\r\nnotes = \"\"\"source - the session log and its telemetry commit are written through the shared primitives' writer, and the raw stream to the untracked run-logs directory a caller names.\"\"\"\r\n\r\n[interface.IF-283]\r\nrationale = \"The coordinator needs one declared argument surface for an adjudication it starts outside the loop, so the caller, parser and command contract agree on which inputs are admissible.\"\r\nowner = \"scripts/coordinator_adjudicate\"\r\nrequestors = [\"external:coordinator\"]\r\nchannel = \"cli\"\r\ndata = \"adjudicate and act command lines; --route names an enabled entry (default ANTHROPIC-OPUS-STRONG@ADJUDICATOR); act --verdict PATH --wi WI-N [--route ID] [--root DIR] [--timeout SECONDS]; signin reads that entry account; --retained reports off without probing when retention is off; adjudicate carries wi\"\r\nversion = \"v1\"\r\nstatus = \"Drafted\"\r\ncomponent = \"CMP-008\"\r\nnotes = \"No tie-back: a coordinator invokes this local command from its own repository session; the locked frame declares no inbound crossing for that invocation. source - adjudicate uses the enabled default route when none is given and signin creates no home.\"\r\n\r\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
