 the coverage gap below.\n\nAnchors judged: DevStg-Reqs, DevStg-Tests, DevStg-Impl, G4, B1, B2, B3, B4. The rows identify concrete deliverables, and the multiple clause citations mostly express genuine test/implementation/record seams. IF-245/246/065 are consumed or amended; the proposed command CLI differs from IF-283'\"'s adjudication argv. The declared order is buildable. \"'`DELTA: within` is supported: the new transcript input and boundary, role/source/scope/outcome values, and cursor/contribution state all have assigned rows. The interruption-recovery coverage is incomplete as described below.\n\nTransfer caveat: the debate/selection evidence behind this protocol comes from QA, math and code with objective verifiers; plan artifacts have not been benchmarked, and reconciliation evaluated for plan quality remains an open research gap. This rubric is an extrapolation, not a proven instrument.\n\n- [MAJOR] DevStg-Tests -> plan decision 5 (lines 320 onward), P4/P5, and P2'\"'s kill/torn-log tests (lines 706–707) do not deliver D4's killed-run recovery. The supported interruption path is explicitly in the spec's Trust section: a spool write can fail or a run can be killed. At this commit \"'`agent_common.write_session_log` writes directly to the final discoverable name with `path.write_text` (line 1597); P4 only adds columns and the plan leaves that writer otherwise unchanged. A kill during that write can leave an empty or unterminated `call_<invocation-id>-*.log`. Every retry discovers it and refuses the invocation, so the required rerun cannot finish recording each invocation once. Raising KeyboardInterrupt on the third `record` call tests interruption between writes, while the torn-log test explicitly blesses permanent refusal. -> Extend P4 to publish completed logs atomically through the existing shared writer, with an incomplete temporary file outside the final call-log pattern; add an interrupted-write/retry test proving the final log is either absent or complete and the rerun produces exactly one complete contribution. Preserve refusal for genuinely unreadable previously published logs. -> @implementer\n\nVERDICT: CHANGES-REQUESTED findings=1\n'\"'@\nNew-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path (Split-Path -Parent \"'$verdictPath) | Out-Null\n[System.IO.File]::WriteAllText($verdictPath, $verdictText.Replace(\"`r`n\", \"`n\") + \"`n\", [System.Text.UTF8Encoding]::new($false))\nGet-Content -LiteralPath $verdictPath | Select-Object -First 1\nGet-Content -LiteralPath $verdictPath | Select-Object -Last 1'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
